id: pm-1j5j21
title: "GH-921/GH-922: merge-decision receipts are not durable in fresh-clone CI"
description: "Pending merge-decision receipts live only in clone-local ignored state, so a fresh checkout cannot distinguish a lossy concurrent merge; history-repair can erase the last tracked drift signal and make discarded work pass strict health."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T08:33:38.852Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-09T15:58:32.674Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-09T15:57:23.719Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-09T15:57:23.719Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Merge-decision receipts required by validation survive a fresh clone and clean CI checkout without relying on ignored local files; the field-aware merge driver and health/validate surfaces agree on durable evidence; isolated two-branch merge tests cover both lossless and discarded-value decisions and keep history hash validation intact
parent: pm-doxj
risk: critical
confidence: high
severity: critical
resolution: "Persisted privacy-safe hash-only merge decision receipt sidecars inside the project tracker while retaining raw values only in clone-local Git state; listing, health, validation, and reconciliation now merge both sources deterministically."
expected_result: Merge decision evidence must survive a fresh clone without committing raw conflicting values or losing local reconciliation capability.
actual_result: "Fresh clones retain stable hash-only decision evidence, original clones retain raw-value receipts, duplicate receipt identities prefer local detail, and reconciliation updates both stores."
affected_version: 2026.8.6
component: merge safety and durable history
